findings.body:
When a user with `IdentityProvider.CAL` and 2FA enabled later signs in via Google or SAML (lines 694–711), their `identityProvider` is updated to `GOOGLE`/`SAML` while `twoFactorEnabled` remains `true`, and login redirects to `/auth/login?totp=<jwt>` (`totpEmail`).

In `authorize` (lines 113–119), the checks:
```ts
if (user.identityProvider !== IdentityProvider.CAL && !credentials.totpCode) {
  throw new Error(ErrorCode.ThirdPartyIdentityProviderEnabled);
}
```
only exempt `credentials.totpCode` and not `credentials.backupCode`. If such a user attempts to authenticate with a backup code (where `credentials.totpCode` is empty), `authorize` throws `ErrorCode.ThirdPartyIdentityProviderEnabled` before reaching the backup code verification on line 131. Additionally, `ExternalTotpFooter` in `apps/web/pages/auth/login.tsx` (lines 135–143, 180) does not render the "Lost access" button when `totpEmail` is set.
